    {
      "waived": "a modal scrim over a dark ground. This is a transient STATE, not a resting surface, and suppressing the background is the scrim doing its job. The geometry leaves no alternative: the ground is already CIE L* 8.6, so any scrim pushes parts of it below L* 5 — which is why the dark scrim is already down to alpha 0.34. What has to be comfortable in this state is the dialog, and the content-plane metrics covering it pass: mean L* 10.0-16.8, brightness step 8-13, zero glare. The light-mode scrim was a real defect and was fixed rather than waived — it washed the page maroon at alpha 0.55 and now measures inside the bar at all four widths.",
